  },
  "analysis": {
    "unit": "workload seed (paired across all conditions)",
    "ci": "paired 95% Student t",
    "test": "two-sided sign-flip: exact for lattice-valued differences, otherwise Monte Carlo with 1,000,000 draws (seed 20261120)",
    "multiplicity": "Holm within each family; B_primary (4 tests) is confirmatory; B_service_scale (4 tests) is a prespecified secondary family; others secondary/descriptive",
    "margin_rule": "A 95% CI inside +/- margin is reported as 'no effect larger than the margin'; Holm p < 0.05 with CI outside the margin as 'effect exceeding the margin'; Holm p < 0.05 with CI inside as 'detectable but below the margin'; anything else as 'inconclusive'.",
    "effect_sizes": "mean paired contrast, 95% CI, SD, d_z"
  },
  "sample_size": "n = 40 seeds (960 runs). From the 320-run campaign: SD of the per-seed alpha x SOC interaction on completions 2.0-2.9 per 100, and SD of the 25% SOC service loss 2.3-2.5 per 100. At n = 40 the 95% CI half-width is about 0.65-0.92 per 100 for the interaction and about 0.8 for the service-loss contrasts, enough to place intervals inside the +/-1 margin when the true value is near 0, and to detect a service-loss change of 2 per 100 with power > 0.9 at Holm alpha 0.0125.",
